I've reviewed the code. It is structured correctly and there are no critical syntax errors. However, there is one major **runtime stability issue** common with Generative AI apps:

**The JSON Parsing Risk:**
The Gemini API (especially the Flash model) sometimes wraps JSON responses in Markdown code blocks (e.g., ` ```json { ... } ``` `), even when `responseMimeType: 'application/json'` is set. Using `JSON.parse(response.text)` directly on this will cause the app to crash with a `SyntaxError`.

I will patch `services/geminiService.ts` to include a helper that strips Markdown before parsing.

# Updated files:

## services/geminiService.ts

Added a `cleanAndParseJSON` helper function to safely strip Markdown code blocks (```json ... ```) from the AI response before parsing. This prevents the app from crashing if the AI formats the output as a code snippet.

```typescript
// Helper to safely parse JSON that might be wrapped in markdown
const cleanAndParseJSON = (text: string) => {
    if (!text) return {};
    let clean = text.trim();
    // Remove markdown code blocks if present
    if (clean.startsWith('```')) {
        clean = clean.replace(/^```(json)?\n/, '').replace(/\n```$/, '');
    }
    // Remove any trailing/leading whitespace again
    clean = clean.trim();
    try {
        return JSON.parse(clean);
    } catch (e) {
        console.error("JSON Parse Error:", e, "Input text:", text);
        return {};
    }
};
```

This logic is applied to `generateWardrobe`, `generateSceneScript`, and `analyzeGarment`.

